.TH EXPANSE 3 "2026-08-27" "libexpanse" "Expanse C Library Manual"
.SH NAME
expanse \- modern Judy arrays and high-performance digital tree engine
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <expanse.h>
.PP
.BI "const char *expanse_version(void);"
.PP
Link with \fI-lexpanse\fR.
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBlibexpanse\fR is a clean-room, modernized C library implementation of
Judy arrays and digital trees (radix tries) designed for high-density
cache-conscious indexing.
It provides both modern, strongly-typed C APIs (\fBexpanse.h\fR) and drop-in
binary compatibility for legacy \fBlibjudy\fR applications (\fBJudy.h\fR).
.PP
Digital trees in Expanse partition keys by \fBexpanse\fR (byte digit positions
from MSB to LSB) rather than population, dynamically adapting node structures
between zero-allocation immediates, linear arrays, POPCNT-indexed bitmapped
nodes, and uncompressed arrays.
.SH CONTAINER TYPES
.TP
.BR expanse_set_t " (see " expanse_set (3))
Dynamic sparse 64-bit unsigned integer set (analogous to Judy1).
.TP
.BR expanse_map_t " (see " expanse_map (3))
Dynamic ordered map from 64-bit unsigned integer keys to 64-bit values
(analogous to JudyL).
.TP
.BR expanse_strmap_t " (see " expanse_strmap (3))
Dynamic ordered map from null-terminated C strings to 64-bit values
(analogous to JudySL).
.TP
.BR expanse_bytesmap_t " (see " expanse_bytesmap (3))
Dynamic map from arbitrary byte slices to 64-bit values
(analogous to JudyHS).
.TP
.BR expanse_sync_set_t ", " expanse_sync_map_t " (see " expanse_sync (3))
Concurrent set and map supporting single-writer mutations with lock-free
Optimistic Concurrency Control (OCC) reader handles.
.TP
.BR ExpanseBlobMap " (see " expanse_blob_map (3))
Polymorphic large-value map with inline payload packing and slab arena
allocation.
.SH QUICK REFERENCE
.nf
.ta 22n 18n 40n
\fBContainer Type\fR	\fBKey Type\fR	\fBValue Type / Features\fR
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
expanse_set_t	uint64_t	Bit set; rank & select; batch query
expanse_map_t	uint64_t	uint64_t; direct slot ptr; rank/select
expanse_strmap_t	const char *	uint64_t; lexicographic order
expanse_bytesmap_t	void * + len	uint64_t; arbitrary byte buffers
expanse_sync_set_t	uint64_t	Lock-free concurrent readers (OCC)
expanse_sync_map_t	uint64_t	uint64_t; lock-free readers (OCC)
ExpanseBlobMap	uint64_t	Arbitrary bytes; arena slab
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
The following complete C program demonstrates creating a map, inserting
key-value pairs, retrieving values, performing range queries, and freeing
the container:
.PP
.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <stdint.h>
#include <inttypes.h>
#include <expanse.h>

int main(void) {
    printf("libexpanse version: %s\\n", expanse_version());

    expanse_map_t *map = expanse_map_new();
    if (!map) {
        fprintf(stderr, "Allocation failed\\n");
        return 1;
    }

    /* Insert keys */
    expanse_map_insert(map, 100, 1000, NULL);
    expanse_map_insert(map, 250, 2500, NULL);
    expanse_map_insert(map, 500, 5000, NULL);

    /* Point lookup */
    uint64_t val;
    if (expanse_map_get(map, 250, &val)) {
        printf("Key 250 -> %" PRIu64 "\\n", val);
    }

    /* Rank: count keys in range [100, 300] */
    uint64_t count = expanse_map_count_range(map, 100, 300);
    printf("Keys in [100, 300]: %" PRIu64 "\\n", count);

    /* Sorted iteration */
    uint64_t k = 0, v = 0;
    if (expanse_map_first(map, &k, &v)) {
        do {
            printf("  %" PRIu64 " -> %" PRIu64 "\\n", k, v);
        } while (expanse_map_next_after(map, k, &k, &v));
    }

    printf("Memory used: %zu bytes\\n", expanse_map_mem_used(map));
    expanse_map_free(map);
    return 0;
}
.fi
.SH CONCURRENCY & THREAD SAFETY
Distinct container handles are completely independent and may be accessed
concurrently from different threads without coordination.
.PP
For concurrent access to a single shared container across multiple threads,
use \fBexpanse_sync_set_t\fR or \fBexpanse_sync_map_t\fR (see
\fBexpanse_sync\fR(3)), which provide lock-free reader handles utilizing
Optimistic Concurrency Control (OCC) and Epoch-Based Reclamation (EBR).
.SH COMPATIBILITY
\fBlibexpanse\fR also provides full drop-in C ABI compatibility for classic
\fBlibjudy\fR.
Legacy programs can include \fB<Judy.h>\fR and link with \fI-lexpanse\fR
without source modifications (see \fBJudy\fR(3)).
